Project Aloha RamPartitionDxe: let the RAM above 0x180000000 join the EFI
memory map entry of the PEI-declared RAM just below it.

AddRamPartition() added the RAM it reads from SMEM with GCD capabilities 0xF,
while the PEI map (PlatformMemoryMapLib, SYS_MEM_CAP) gives system memory
UC|WC|WT|WB|RP|WP|XP and CpuDxe adds RO. The DXE core merges adjacent free
ranges only when their attributes match, so on xiaomi-andromeda (6 GiB)
0x140000000-0x180000000 and 0x180000000-0x200000000 stayed two descriptors
and DarwinBoot's AllocatePages(AllocateAddress) across 0x180000000 failed
with EFI_NOT_FOUND. With the capabilities of the region below, the two merge
into one 3 GiB conventional run.

Applied by scripts/firmware-in-container.sh (apply_once). Upstream code:
Kancy Joe (sunflower2333) and XiaoYeZi (qaz6750), Project Aloha.

diff --git a/Platforms/AndromedaPkg/Driver/RamPartitionDxe/RamPartitionDxe.c b/Platforms/AndromedaPkg/Driver/RamPartitionDxe/RamPartitionDxe.c
index 9fd719a3..6b8192b7 100644
--- a/Platforms/AndromedaPkg/Driver/RamPartitionDxe/RamPartitionDxe.c
+++ b/Platforms/AndromedaPkg/Driver/RamPartitionDxe/RamPartitionDxe.c
@@ -134,6 +134,9 @@ AddRamPartition(
 {
   EFI_STATUS          Status           = EFI_SUCCESS;
   EFI_GCD_MEMORY_TYPE EfiGcdMemoryType = EfiGcdMemoryTypeReserved;
+  UINT64              Capabilities     = EFI_MEMORY_UC | EFI_MEMORY_WC |
+                                         EFI_MEMORY_WT | EFI_MEMORY_WB;
+  EFI_GCD_MEMORY_SPACE_DESCRIPTOR Below;
 
   switch (EfiMemoryType) {
   case EfiReservedMemoryType:
@@ -153,9 +156,27 @@ AddRamPartition(
   if (Length == 0)
     return EFI_INVALID_PARAMETER;
 
+  //
+  // RAM that continues the system memory just below it gets the same GCD
+  // capabilities (the PEI-declared UC|WC|WT|WB|RP|WP|XP, to which CpuDxe
+  // has already added RO). The DXE core uses them as the EFI memory map attribute
+  // and only merges adjacent free ranges whose attributes match: with a
+  // fixed 0xF the RAM from 0x180000000 stayed a separate descriptor from the
+  // PEI "RAM Partition" below it, so AllocatePages(AllocateAddress) could not
+  // take a range across 0x180000000 ("covers multiple entries"). The old
+  // capabilities stay a subset, so the attribute calls below still apply.
+  //
+  if ((EfiGcdMemoryType == EfiGcdMemoryTypeSystemMemory) && (Base != 0) &&
+      !EFI_ERROR(gDS->GetMemorySpaceDescriptor(Base - 1, &Below)) &&
+      (Below.GcdMemoryType == EfiGcdMemoryTypeSystemMemory) &&
+      ((Below.Capabilities & Capabilities) == Capabilities)) {
+    Capabilities = Below.Capabilities & ~EFI_MEMORY_RUNTIME;
+  }
+
   DEBUG(
-      (EFI_D_ERROR, "Adding Memory Space: 0x%08llx 0x%08llx\n", Base, Length));
-  Status = gDS->AddMemorySpace(EfiGcdMemoryType, Base, Length, 0xF);
+      (EFI_D_ERROR, "Adding Memory Space: 0x%08llx 0x%08llx caps 0x%llx\n",
+       Base, Length, Capabilities));
+  Status = gDS->AddMemorySpace(EfiGcdMemoryType, Base, Length, Capabilities);
   if (EFI_ERROR(Status)) {
     DEBUG((EFI_D_ERROR, "AddMemorySpace Failed ! %r\n", Status));
     return Status;
